   "daf": "89a",
   "sentenceId": 15,
   "he": "הִין – תְּרֵיסַר לוּגֵּי הָוַיִין, דִּכְתִיב: ״שֶׁמֶן זַיִת הִין״, וּכְתִיב: ״שֶׁמֶן מִשְׁחַת קֹדֶשׁ יִהְיֶה זֶה לִי לְדֹרֹתֵיכֶם״, זֶה בְּגִימַטְרִיָּא תְּרֵיסַר הָוַיִין.",
   "en": "The Gemara elaborates: Now, one «hin is twelve log, as it is written: “And of olive oil a hin”» (Exodus 30:24), «and it is written» afterward in the same verse: «“Sacred anointing oil, this [zeh] shall be for Me, throughout your generations.”» The «numerical value [gimatriyya] of zeh is twelve.» Once it is established that one hin is twelve log, it is possible to calculate how may log are in one-half, one-third, and one-quarter of a hin."
  }
